d/gates.py\", \"src/superclaude/cli/prd/prompts.py\"],\n      \"why\": \"The PRD pipeline has multiple schema constants that could drift: _RESEARCH_REQUIRED_SECTIONS (7 sections), _PRD_CRITICAL_SECTIONS (5 sections), and potentially others. The codebase demonstrates a pattern of centralizing shared vocabulary (cli/vocabulary.py for obligation terms). The PRD pipeline would benefit from a similar schemas.py module to avoid duplication and drift. The round-trip test is a mitigation but does not eliminate the duplication.\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Create src/superclaude/cli/prd/schemas.py to hold _RESEARCH_REQUIRED_SECTIONS and _PRD_CRITICAL_SECTIONS as exportable constants. Import these in gates.py and prompts.py. This follows the established vocabulary.py pattern and makes the single-source-of-truth explicit.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Prompt-gate contract validation is test-only, not runtime\",\n      \"category\": \"architecture\",\n      \"severity_hint\": \"low\",\n      \"affected_files\": [\"tests/cli/prd/test_research_notes_roundtrip.py\", \"src/superclaude/cli/prd/executor.py\"],\n      \"why\": \"The round-trip test validates prompt-gate alignment at test time, but the pipeline executor does not perform any runtime validation. If gates.py is edited incorrectly and tests are not run (or are skipped), the pipeline will fail at runtime with opaque gate failures. Other pipelines (cli_portify, roadmap) have similar test-only validation. This is acceptable for development, but a production deployment with schema drift could fail silently.\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Consider adding a startup self-check in the executor or CLI entry point that validates critical schema invariants (e.g., _RESEARCH_REQUIRED_SECTIONS has exactly 7 elements). This is a 'sanity check' pattern, not a replacement for tests, but catches configuration errors before pipeline execution.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"low\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"not